#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Note:** Qiskit loosely describes "
"[layers](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/api/qiskit/qiskit.dagcircuit.DAGCircuit)"
" as being depth-1 partitions of the circuit across all qubits. This package "
"makes use of the term **slices** to describe layers of arbitrary depth. The "
"[qiskit_addon_obp.backpropagate](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"obp/stubs/qiskit_addon_obp.backpropagate.html) function is designed to "
"backpropagate entire slices at a time, so the choice of how to slice the "
"quantum circuit can have a major impact on how well backpropagation performs"
" for a given problem. You will lean more about **slices** below.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Nota:** Qiskit describe informalmente las "
"[capas](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/api/qiskit/qiskit.dagcircuit.DAGCircuit)"
" como particiones de profundidad 1 del circuito sobre todos los qubits. Este"
" paquete usa el término **slices** para describir capas de profundidad "
"arbitraria. La función "
"[qiskit_addon_obp.backpropagate](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"obp/stubs/qiskit_addon_obp.backpropagate.html) está diseñada para "
"retropropagar slices completos a la vez, por lo que la elección de cómo "
"dividir el circuito cuántico puede tener un impacto importante en el "
"rendimiento de la retropropagación para un problema dado. Aprenderás más "
"sobre los **slices** a continuación.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map to quantum problem {#step-1-map-to-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Paso 1: Mapear al problema cuántico {#step-1-map-to-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Map the time-evolution of a quantum Heisenberg model to a quantum "
"experiment. {#map-the-time-evolution-of-a-quantum-heisenberg-model-to-a-"
"quantum-experiment}"
msgstr ""
"Mapear la evolución temporal de un modelo cuántico de Heisenberg a un "
"experimento cuántico. {#map-the-time-evolution-of-a-quantum-heisenberg-"
"model-to-a-quantum-experiment}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The [qiskit_addon_utils](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/) "
"package provides some reusable functionalities for various purposes.\n"
msgstr ""
"El paquete [qiskit_addon_utils](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"utils/) proporciona algunas funcionalidades reutilizables para diversos "
"propósitos.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Its [qiskit_addon_utils.problem_generators](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/stubs/qiskit_addon_utils.problem_generators.html) module provides functions to generate Heisenberg-like Hamiltonians on a given connectivity graph.\n"
"This graph can be either a [rustworkx.PyGraph](https://www.rustworkx.org/apiref/rustworkx.PyGraph.html) or a [CouplingMap](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap) making it easy to use in Qiskit-centric workflows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Su módulo [qiskit_addon_utils.problem_generators](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/stubs/qiskit_addon_utils.problem_generators.html) ofrece funciones para generar Hamiltonianos tipo Heisenberg sobre un grafo de conectividad dado.\n"
"Este grafo puede ser un [rustworkx.PyGraph](https://www.rustworkx.org/apiref/rustworkx.PyGraph.html) o un [CouplingMap](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap), lo que facilita su uso en flujos de trabajo centrados en Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the following, we first generate a heavy-hex `CouplingMap` out of which "
"we carve a linear chain of 10 qubits. Note, that the indices of this new "
"`reduced_coupling_map` are again zero-based.\n"
msgstr ""
"A continuación, primero generamos un `CouplingMap` heavy-hex del que "
"extraemos una cadena lineal de 10 qubits. Ten en cuenta que los índices de "
"este nuevo `reduced_coupling_map` vuelven a comenzar desde cero.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "![Code output](/img/qiskit-addons/obp/01-getting-started/output_1.png)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Code output](/img/qiskit-addons/obp/01-getting-started/output_1.png)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we generate a Pauli operator modeling a Heisenberg XYZ Hamiltonian.\n"
msgstr ""
"A continuación, generamos un operador de Pauli que modela un Hamiltoniano de"
" Heisenberg XYZ.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\\hat{H} = \\sum_{(j,k)\\in E} (J_{x} \\sigma_j^{x} \\sigma_{k}^{x} +\n"
"    J_{y} \\sigma_j^{y} \\sigma_{k}^{y} + J_{z} \\sigma_j^{z} \\sigma_{k}^{z}) +\n"
"    \\sum_{j\\in V} (h_{x} \\sigma_j^{x} + h_{y} \\sigma_j^{y} + h_{z} \\sigma_j^{z})$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\\hat{H} = \\sum_{(j,k)\\in E} (J_{x} \\sigma_j^{x} \\sigma_{k}^{x} +\n"
"    J_{y} \\sigma_j^{y} \\sigma_{k}^{y} + J_{z} \\sigma_j^{z} \\sigma_{k}^{z}) +\n"
"    \\sum_{j\\in V} (h_{x} \\sigma_j^{x} + h_{y} \\sigma_j^{y} + h_{z} \\sigma_j^{z})$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Where $G(V,E)$ is the graph of the coupling map provided.\n"
msgstr "Donde $G(V,E)$ es el grafo del mapa de acoplamiento proporcionado.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"From the qubit operator, we can generate a quantum circuit which models its time evolution.\n"
"Once again, the [qiskit_addon_utils.problem_generators](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/stubs/qiskit_addon_utils.problem_generators.html) module comes to the resuce with a handy function do just that:\n"
msgstr ""
"A partir del operador de qubits, podemos generar un circuito cuántico que modela su evolución temporal.\n"
"Una vez más, el módulo [qiskit_addon_utils.problem_generators](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/stubs/qiskit_addon_utils.problem_generators.html) viene al rescate con una función práctica para hacer exactamente eso:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/obp/01-getting-"
"started/output_2.png)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/obp/01-getting-"
"started/output_2.png)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize the problem {#step-2-optimize-the-problem}"
msgstr "Paso 2: Optimizar el problema {#step-2-optimize-the-problem}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Create circuit slices to backpropagate {#create-circuit-slices-to-"
"backpropagate}"
msgstr ""
"Crear slices del circuito para retropropagar {#create-circuit-slices-to-"
"backpropagate}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Remember, the ``backpropagate`` function will backpropagate entire circuit "
"slices at a time, so the choice of how to slice can have an impact on how "
"well backpropagation performs for a given problem. Here, we will group gates"
" of the same type into slices using the "
"[slice_by_gate_types](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"utils/stubs/qiskit_addon_utils.slicing.slice_by_gate_types.html) function.\n"
msgstr ""
"Recuerda que la función ``backpropagate`` retropropagará slices completos "
"del circuito a la vez, por lo que la elección de cómo dividirlo puede "
"afectar el rendimiento de la retropropagación para un problema dado. Aquí, "
"agruparemos las compuertas del mismo tipo en slices usando la función "
"[slice_by_gate_types](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"utils/stubs/qiskit_addon_utils.slicing.slice_by_gate_types.html).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a more detailed discussion on circuit slicing, check out this [how-to "
"guide](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"utils/how_tos/create_circuit_slices.html) of the [qiskit-addon-"
"utils](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/index.html) package.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para una discusión más detallada sobre la división del circuito en slices, "
"consulta esta [guía práctica](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"utils/how_tos/create_circuit_slices.html) del paquete [qiskit-addon-"
"utils](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/index.html).\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Constrain how large the operator may grow during backpropagation "
"{#constrain-how-large-the-operator-may-grow-during-backpropagation}"
msgstr ""
"Limitar el tamaño máximo que puede alcanzar el operador durante la "
"retropropagación {#constrain-how-large-the-operator-may-grow-during-"
"backpropagation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"During backpropagation, the number of terms in the operator will generally "
"approach $4^N$ quickly, where $N$ is the number of qubits. The size of the "
"operator can be bounded by specifying the ``operator_budget`` kwarg of the "
"``backpropagate`` function, which accepts an "
"[OperatorBudget](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"obp/stubs/qiskit_addon_obp.utils.simplify.OperatorBudget.html) instance.\n"
msgstr ""
"Durante la retropropagación, el número de términos en el operador "
"generalmente se aproxima rápidamente a $4^N$, donde $N$ es el número de "
"qubits. El tamaño del operador puede acotarse especificando el argumento "
"``operator_budget`` de la función ``backpropagate``, que acepta una "
"instancia de [OperatorBudget](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"obp/stubs/qiskit_addon_obp.utils.simplify.OperatorBudget.html).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we specify that backpropagation should stop when the number of qubit-"
"wise commuting Pauli groups in the operator grows past 8.\n"
msgstr ""
"Aquí especificamos que la retropropagación debe detenerse cuando el número "
"de grupos de Pauli con conmutación qubit a qubit en el operador supere 8.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Backpropagate slices from the circuit {#backpropagate-slices-from-the-"
"circuit}"
msgstr ""
"Retropropagar slices del circuito {#backpropagate-slices-from-the-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, we will specify the Pauli-Z observable on qubit 0, and we will "
"backpropagate slices from the time-evolution circuit until the terms in the "
"observable can no longer be combined into 8 or fewer qubit-wise commuting "
"Pauli groups.\n"
msgstr ""
"Primero, especificaremos el observable de Pauli-Z en el qubit 0, y "
"retropropagaremos slices del circuito de evolución temporal hasta que los "
"términos del observable ya no puedan combinarse en 8 o menos grupos de Pauli"
" con conmutación qubit a qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Below you will see that we backpropagated 7 slices but only used 6 of the 8 "
"allotted Pauli groups. This implies that backpropagating one more slice "
"would cause the number of Pauli groups to exceed 8. We can verify that this "
"is the case by inspecting the returned metadata.\n"
msgstr ""
"A continuación verás que retropropagamos 7 slices pero solo usamos 6 de los "
"8 grupos de Pauli disponibles. Esto implica que retropropagar un slice más "
"haría que el número de grupos de Pauli superara 8. Podemos verificar que "
"este es el caso inspeccionando los metadatos devueltos.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/obp/01-getting-"
"started/output_3.png)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/obp/01-getting-"
"started/output_3.png)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we will specify the same problem with the same constraints on the size"
" of the output observable. However, this time, we allot an error budget to "
"each slice using the [setup_budet](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"obp/stubs/qiskit_addon_obp.utils.truncating.setup_budget.html) function. "
"Pauli terms with small coefficients will be truncated from each slice until "
"the error budget is filled, and leftover budget will be added to the "
"following slice's budget.\n"
msgstr ""
"A continuación, especificaremos el mismo problema con las mismas "
"restricciones sobre el tamaño del observable de salida. Sin embargo, esta "
"vez asignaremos un presupuesto de error a cada slice usando la función "
"[setup_budet](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"obp/stubs/qiskit_addon_obp.utils.truncating.setup_budget.html). Los términos"
" de Pauli con coeficientes pequeños se truncarán de cada slice hasta agotar "
"el presupuesto de error, y el presupuesto restante se añadirá al presupuesto"
" del siguiente slice.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In order to enable this truncation, we need to setup our error budget like "
"so:\n"
msgstr ""
"Para habilitar este truncamiento, necesitamos configurar nuestro presupuesto"
" de error de la siguiente manera:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that by allocating `5e-3` error per slice for truncation, we are able "
"to remove 3 more slices from the circuit, while remaining within the "
"original budget of 8 commuting Pauli groups in the observable. By default, "
"`backpropagate` uses the L1 norm of the truncated coefficients to bound the "
"total error incurred from truncation. For other options refer to the [how-to"
" guide on specifying the p_norm](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"obp/how_tos/bound_error_using_p_norm.html).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ten en cuenta que al asignar `5e-3` de error por slice para el truncamiento,"
" podemos eliminar 3 slices más del circuito, manteniéndonos dentro del "
"presupuesto original de 8 grupos de Pauli conmutativos en el observable. Por"
" defecto, `backpropagate` usa la norma L1 de los coeficientes truncados para"
" acotar el error total incurrido por el truncamiento. Para otras opciones, "
"consulta la [guía práctica sobre cómo especificar la "
"p_norm](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"obp/how_tos/bound_error_using_p_norm.html).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this particular example where we have backpropagated 10 slices, the total truncation error should not exceed ``(5e-3 error/slice) * (10 slices) = 5e-2``.\n"
"For further discussion on distributing an error budget across your slices, check out [this how-to guide](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-obp/how_tos/truncate_operator_terms.html).\n"
msgstr ""
"En este ejemplo particular donde hemos retropropagado 10 slices, el error total de truncamiento no debería superar ``(5e-3 error/slice) * (10 slices) = 5e-2``.\n"
"Para más información sobre cómo distribuir un presupuesto de error entre los slices, consulta [esta guía práctica](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-obp/how_tos/truncate_operator_terms.html).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/obp/01-getting-"
"started/output_4.png)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/obp/01-getting-"
"started/output_4.png)\n"

